{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1400","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Zigzags"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a_1, a_2 \\dots a_n$$$. Calculate the number of tuples $$$(i, j, k, l)$$$ such that: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 \\le i \\lt j \\lt k \\lt l \\le n$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$a_i = a_k$$$ and $$$a_j = a_l$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$4 \\le n \\le 3000$$$) — the size of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le n$$$) — the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ in one test doesn't exceed $$$3000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the number of described tuples."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n5\n2 2 2 2 2\n6\n1 3 3 1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, for any four indices $$$i \\lt j \\lt k \\lt l$$$ are valid, so the answer is the number of tuples."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, there are $$$2$$$ valid tuples: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(1, 2, 4, 6)$$$: $$$a_1 = a_4$$$ and $$$a_2 = a_6$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(1, 3, 4, 6)$$$: $$$a_1 = a_4$$$ and $$$a_3 = a_6$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1400D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1400/problem/D"}